# Mirrors .railwayignore — Railway's Railpack builder goes through a
# container-image build even without a literal Dockerfile, and some
# build backends respect .dockerignore specifically rather than
# .railwayignore. Keeping both means whichever one Railway actually
# reads, the machine-local node_modules/build-cache junk stays out of
# the image either way.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

dist/
**/dist/
build/
**/build/

.git/

.turbo/
**/.turbo/
.vite/
**/.vite/
coverage/
**/coverage/
playwright-report/
test-results/

apps/server/storage/
apps/server/prisma/dev.db
*.log

.env
.env.local
.vercel/
